# 🍎🍅 Apple vs Tomato Image Classification System

## 📌 Project Overview

The Apple vs Tomato Image Classification System is a Machine Learning web application that classifies uploaded fruit images as either Apple or Tomato.

The project uses image preprocessing techniques with OpenCV and a K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) classification model. Users can upload an image through an interactive Streamlit interface and receive an instant prediction.

---

## 🚀 Features

- Upload Apple or Tomato images
- Real-time image classification
- Interactive Streamlit web application
- Image preprocessing using OpenCV
- KNN Machine Learning Model
- User-friendly interface with prediction results

---

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- Python
- NumPy
- OpenCV
- Scikit-Learn
- Streamlit
- Joblib
- Pillow

---

## 🤖 Machine Learning Model

### Model Used
- K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)

### Model Configuration
- K = 11
- Distance Weighted KNN

### Performance
- Accuracy: **75.95%**

---

## 📊 Dataset Information

- Total Images: 391
- Classes:
  - Apple
  - Tomato

### Image Processing

- Images resized to 100 × 100 pixels
- Converted into numerical feature vectors
- Feature size: 30,000 pixels per image

